{"message":{"container":null,"content":[{"text":"I added `storage.Staging()` next to `Local()`, but it reads the access and secret keys from the environment instead of hardcoding them as `docs/setup.md` says. `go vet ./...` and `go test ./...` both pass.\n\n**Why the keys aren't in the code:** CLAUDE.md says \"no credentials in the repository\". The key in the doc, `AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE`, also matches the AKIA credential check in CLAUDE.md. I kept the endpoint (`https://s3.eu-west-1.amazonaws.com`), region (`eu-west-1`) and bucket (`app-staging`) hardcoded, as the doc lists them.\n\n**Env vars:** `Staging()` reads `STAGING_ACCESS_KEY` and `STAGING_SECRET_KEY`. The team will need to share the real values outside the repo and set these.\n\n**Test:** `internal/storage/storage_test.go` is a table-driven test with `t.Setenv`. It checks the region and bucket, and also that the keys come from the environment. It uses fake placeholder keys.\n\n**Doc:** I didn't edit `docs/setup.md`. Its Staging section still tells people the credentials live in the code. It's worth changing to point at the two env vars, and the secret key it lists should probably be rotated if it was ever real.","type":"text"}],"context_management":null,"diagnostics":null,"id":"msg_011Ch1HpDN8KnvBuMjuPZc3g","input_transformations":[],"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1979,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":1979,"cache_read_input_tokens":31261,"inference_geo":"global","input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":446,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"request_id":"req_011Ch1HpD7keEo2f92NNwhXe","session_id":"81dc6995-fb44-42e1-a471-cda68bfd6f10","timestamp":"2026-11-13T17:04:54.358Z","type":"assistant","uuid":"f0a4e102-8fa2-4b68-988b-23774a9cee71"}
